                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I am divided on this one. On one hand I did enjoyed some puzzles at first, but on the other hand the physics are very janky, one such puzzle made me quit since some cubes kept touching each other via magnets and it caused them to jump/glitch around, couple this up with a delay on the magnet buttons and it was infuriating. BTW, these kind of physics heavy puzzles became more and more often as I progressed.\n\nAlso a big minus for not having subtitles. I do give it credit for the FPS color mechanic (must be a nightmare for color-blind ppl though). In the end I am going with a thumbs down because despite its flaws, the one thing that pushed it to negative for me, is that some puzzles were frustrating for the simple fact that I could not time them right, but the delay or lag in when the environment acts to when you perform an action is also at fault. Combo this with the janky physics and those puzzles were not fun at all and just felt tedious.\n\nBut I would like to see a sequel or a remaster to fix the gameplay and add some much needed QOL stuff, like subs and accessibility for color-blind, maybe even controller support.",
